# Contributing

This page defines the focused change and review workflow for `{{ service_name }}`.

## Before editing

Read the repository [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) and service-owned [`SERVICE.md`](../../SERVICE.md), then inspect the current implementation and the canonical documentation for the area being changed. `SERVICE.md` defines concrete responsibilities; the pristine scaffold must not gain unrelated business behavior.

Use the template and `pypokerlost` primitives that already own a concern. Do not introduce an alternative HTTP transport, transaction manager, configuration framework, dependency-injection system, or deployment workflow when an established primitive satisfies the requirement.

## Scope discipline

- Keep each change focused on the requested responsibility.
- Do not mix broad formatting or unrelated renaming with a behavior change.
- Preserve layer boundaries and public contracts unless the task explicitly changes them.
- Add infrastructure or dependencies only for a concrete service responsibility.
- Update the one canonical documentation page for every affected concept.
- Follow the [Python style](python-style.md) and [documentation style](documentation-style.md) guides.

An API change must also update the [public surface manifest](../api/public-surface.md) and the relevant canonical API page. Wire-contract changes require the SDK/OpenAPI compatibility workflow described in [OpenAPI and SDK](../api/openapi-and-sdk.md).

## Verification

Run the regular checks from the repository root:

```bash
make check
make pre-commit
```

Run explicit database, Docker, Helm, or SDK/OpenAPI checks when the changed area requires them. Do not report a check as passing unless it was executed successfully in the current environment.

Before handing off a change, inspect `git status --short`, run `git diff --check`, and review the complete tracked and untracked diff. Do not rewrite shared Git history as part of ordinary review.
